IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ita-types`
IMPORT `ita-rates`
IMPORT `ita-reliefs`

-- Income Tax Act 1947 — TESTS: RATES, REBATES, REMISSIONS, RESIDENCE, RELIEFS.
-- Expected values worked by hand from ../source/ITA1947.txt (ss 2, 38-43,
-- 92J, 92L, Second and Fifth Schedules); arithmetic shown where not obvious.

§ `Tests — rates and reliefs`

§§ `Residence (s 2)`

GIVEN resides IS A BOOLEAN, days IS A NUMBER, work IS A NUMBER, cm IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Residence facts`
`residence` resides days work cm MEANS `Residence facts` WITH `resides in Singapore, except reasonable temporary absences` IS resides, `days physically present in Singapore` IS days, `days exercising an employment in Singapore, other than as a director` IS work, `control and management of the business exercised in Singapore` IS cm

#ASSERT     `resident in Singapore:` `an individual` `,` (`residence` FALSE 183 0 FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `resident in Singapore:` `an individual` `,` (`residence` FALSE 182 0 FALSE)
#ASSERT     `resident in Singapore:` `an individual` `,` (`residence` FALSE 100 183 FALSE)
#ASSERT     `resident in Singapore:` `an individual` `,` (`residence` TRUE 30 0 FALSE)
#ASSERT     `resident in Singapore:` `a company` `,` (`residence` FALSE 0 0 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `resident in Singapore:` `a company` `,` (`residence` FALSE 365 0 FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `resident in Singapore:` `an executor` `,` (`residence` FALSE 0 0 TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the law is encoded for YA` 2023

§§ `The Second Schedule (s 42)`

